---
title: DownLostFrontend · lost up
---
stateDiagram-v2
    direction TB
    classDef ok stroke-width:1.6px
    classDef wait stroke-width:1.6px
    classDef fail stroke-width:1.6px

    [*] --> select : lost up, owner runs
    select --> confirm : [stopped]
    select --> recover : [exited]
    select --> stop : [running]
    stop --> confirm : owner stops
    stop --> reselect : owner gone, once
    reselect --> confirm : [absent]
    reselect --> recover : [exited]
    reselect --> refused : [running]
    recover --> confirm : death proved
    confirm --> done : [stopped]
    confirm --> refused : [not stopped]
    done --> [*]

    note right of reselect
        HACK-2097: the owner stopped
        itself or died after the first
        selection. Before this fix the
        down refused here.
    end note
    note right of done
        Data retained, frontend
        shutdown recovered; hack up
        starts the run again.
    end note
    note left of refused
        INV NoDeadEnd: only a torn
        publication retirement ends
        here, with nothing replayed.
    end note

    class done ok
    class reselect wait
    class recover wait
    class refused fail
